+# Contract: Command-Line Interface (amended)
+
+**Branch**: `002-phone-redaction-out-dir` | **Spec**: [spec.md](../spec.md)
+
+This **amends** [feature 001's CLI contract](../../001-logredact-cli/contracts/cli.md). That document
+remains in force except where this one supersedes it. Recognition rules are specified separately in
+[redaction-rules.md](./redaction-rules.md).
+
+Everything marked *(unchanged)* is restated only where it is needed to read an amended rule; the 001
+contract is the authority for it.
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m logredact [--count] [--out-dir DIR] [FILE ...]
+```
+
+Requires `src/` on `PYTHONPATH`. No installation, configuration file, or network access. Program name
+in all diagnostics is `logredact`.
+
+### Operands and options
+
+| Token | Meaning |
+|-------|---------|
+| `FILE` | *(unchanged)* A path to read. Read in the exact order given; a repeat is read again |
+| `--count` | *(amended)* Print a four-field tally to stderr after all output. Any position |
+| `--out-dir DIR` | **New.** Write each `FILE`'s redacted lines to `DIR/<basename>` instead of stdout. Any position, any combination with `--count` (FR-019) |
+| anything else beginning with `-` | *(unchanged)* Usage diagnostic on stderr, exit 2 |
+
+`--out-dir` requires **at least one** `FILE` operand (FR-018). `--out-dir` with a missing value is an
+`argparse` usage error: stderr, exit 2.
+
+Without `--out-dir`: zero operands reads standard input and nothing else; one or more operands means
+standard input is not read. *(unchanged)*
+
+With `--out-dir`: standard input is never read, in any case.
+
+## Modes
+
+The option selects one of two output modes for the whole run.
+
+| | Standard-output mode (no `--out-dir`) | Output-folder mode (`--out-dir DIR`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| Redacted text goes to | stdout, all sources concatenated in operand order | `DIR/<basename of operand>`, one file per operand |
+| stdout also carries | nothing else | **only** `wrote N files` (FR-013) |
+| Zero operands | reads stdin | **error**, exit 2 (FR-018) |
+| Byte fidelity | stdout is byte-identical to input but for redactions | each output file is byte-identical to what stdout would have received for that operand (FR-014) |
+
+## Streams
+
+| Stream | Contents |
+|--------|----------|
+| stdin | Log text, read only when no `FILE` operand is given **and** `--out-dir` was not given |
+| stdout | Standard-output mode: every input line, in order, redacted, nothing else altered. Output-folder mode: exactly one `wrote N files` line and nothing else. Never carries the summary |
+| stderr | Nothing at all on a successful run without `--count`; exactly one summary line with `--count`; a diagnostic on failure |
+
+**Ordering guarantee** *(amended)*: within a run, in this order — all redacted output (to stdout or
+to the last output file, which is closed first), then `wrote N files` on stdout in output-folder mode,
+then stdout flushed, then the `--count` summary on stderr (FR-012, FR-007).
+
+**Fidelity guarantee** *(extended to output files)*: for input containing nothing to redact, the
+destination is byte-identical to the concatenated input, including leading/trailing whitespace, `\r`
+before a line ending, bytes that are not valid UTF-8, and the absence of a trailing newline on a
+final line that had none. This now holds for each file written in output-folder mode as well as for
+stdout (FR-014).
+
+**Input immutability**: no `FILE` operand is ever opened for writing, truncated, or modified —
+including when an output path happens to equal an input path (FR-020).
+
+**Determinism** *(unchanged)*: output depends only on input text.
+
+## Summary format *(amended — supersedes 001 FR-017)*
+
+Exactly one line, written to stderr, terminated by `\n`:
+
+```text
+emails=<N> ips=<N> cards=<N> phones=<N>
+```
+
+`phones` is **appended** as a fourth field; the first three keep their names, order and meaning, so a
+consumer parsing them positionally keeps working. Each `<N>` is a decimal count of *replacements
+performed* for that category over all input read in the run — not distinct values, summed across
+every file, and in output-folder mode summed across every output file. Zero is printed as `0`, not
+omitted (FR-006).
+
+## Output-folder status line
+
+Exactly one line, written to **stdout**, terminated by `\n`, only in output-folder mode and only on a
+fully successful run:
+
+```text
+wrote N files
+```
+
+`N` is the number of output files written, counting **one per `FILE` operand** — so on a successful
+run it equals the number of operands, even when two operands share a basename and therefore write the
+same path. The word is literally `files` for every `N`, including `wrote 1 files`; it is not
+pluralised (FR-012, Edge Cases).
+
+## Output file naming and the destination directory
+
+| Rule | Behaviour |
+|------|-----------|
+| Name | `os.path.basename(operand)` — the final name component only; `logs/app.log` → `DIR/app.log` (FR-009) |
+| Missing `DIR` | Created, with every missing parent, before any input is opened (FR-010) |
+| Existing `DIR` | Used as-is; files in it that do not share a name with an operand are untouched (FR-010) |
+| Existing file at the target name | Truncated; none of its previous content survives (FR-011) |
+| Two operands, same basename | Both write the same path, the second replacing the first; one file remains and `N` counts 2 |
+| Empty input file | An empty output file of that name exists; it still counts toward `N` |
+| Operand that cannot be read | **No output file of that name is created** (FR-016) — the input is opened before its output |
+| Earlier operands on a later failure | Their output files are kept (FR-016) |
+
+## Exit statuses *(amended: new failure causes, same two statuses)*
+
+| Status | Condition |
+|--------|-----------|
+| 0 | All requested input was read and all output written successfully (FR-021) |
+| 2 | A named file could not be opened or read (FR-015); **`DIR` could not be created (FR-017)**; **an output file could not be opened, written or closed (FR-017)**; **`--out-dir` was given with zero `FILE` operands (FR-018)**; an unrecognised or malformed option was given; standard output could not be written (broken pipe) |
+
+No other status is produced. Every non-zero exit writes an explanation to stderr naming the offending
+path where one is involved, and produces **no** `--count` summary and **no** `wrote N files` line
+(FR-007, FR-015).
+
+## Diagnostics
+
+Existing rows are unchanged; the new rows are marked.
+
+| Situation | stderr | Exit |
+|-----------|--------|------|
+| File does not exist | `logredact: cannot read 'missing.log': No such file or directory` | 2 |
+| Permission denied | `logredact: cannot read 'secret.log': Permission denied` | 2 |
+| Operand is a directory | `logredact: cannot read 'logs/': Is a directory` | 2 |
+| **`--out-dir` with no operands** | `logredact: --out-dir requires at least one FILE` | 2 |
+| **`DIR` exists as a regular file** | `logredact: cannot write 'clean': File exists` | 2 |
+| **`DIR` cannot be created** | `logredact: cannot write 'clean': <reason>` | 2 |
+| **Output name collides with a subdirectory** | `logredact: cannot write 'clean/app.log': Is a directory` | 2 |
+| **Output file cannot be written** | `logredact: cannot write 'clean/app.log': <reason>` | 2 |
+| Unrecognised option / missing option value | argparse usage block | 2 |
+| stdout closed early | `logredact: cannot write to standard output: Broken pipe` | 2 |
+
+Every path diagnostic names the path **and** the reason (Principle II). Input failures name the
+operand as the user typed it; output failures name the joined output path. The reason text comes from
+the OS error (`OSError.strerror`), so tests match the path and a non-empty reason rather than exact OS
+wording. Attribution is by the operation that raised the error, never inferred from the exception
+(research R7).
+
+## Worked examples
+
+Rows 1–3 are the three invocations in the feature description and are the byte-for-byte checks behind
+SC-001. Rows 4–16 extend the 001 table; the 001 rows remain valid as written, with row 3's stderr
+updated to the four-field form.
+
+| # | Input | Command | stdout | stderr | Exit |
+|---|-------|---------|--------|--------|------|
+| 1 | `call +14155552671 now\n` on stdin | `python -m logredact` | `call [PHONE] now\n` | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 2 | `a@b.io +442071838750\n` on stdin | `python -m logredact --count` | `[EMAIL] [PHONE]\n` | `emails=1 ips=0 cards=0 phones=1\n` | 0 |
+| 3 | `app.log` = `user jane@example.com\n`, `web.log` = `GET / from 10.0.0.7\n` | `python -m logredact --out-dir clean app.log web.log` | `wrote 2 files\n` | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 4 | *(empty)* on stdin | `python -m logredact --count` | *(empty)* | `emails=0 ips=0 cards=0 phones=0\n` | 0 |
+| 5 | `uk +442071838750 us +14155552671\n` | `python -m logredact` | `uk [PHONE] us [PHONE]\n` | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 6 | `ext +1234567\n` | `python -m logredact` | *(input unchanged)* | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 7 | `ref +1234567890123456\n` | `python -m logredact` | *(input unchanged)* | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 8 | `dial 14155552671 please\n` | `python -m logredact` | *(input unchanged)* | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 9 | `+14155552671@example.com\n` | `python -m logredact --count` | `[EMAIL]\n` | `emails=1 ips=0 cards=0 phones=0\n` | 0 |
+| 10 | `+378282246310005\n` | `python -m logredact --count` | `[PHONE]\n` | `emails=0 ips=0 cards=0 phones=1\n` | 0 |
+| 11 | `+4111111111111111\n` | `python -m logredact --count` | `+[CARD]\n` | `emails=0 ips=0 cards=1 phones=0\n` | 0 |
+| 12 | `logs/app.log` readable | `python -m logredact --out-dir clean logs/app.log` | `wrote 1 files\n` | *(empty)* | 0 |
+| 13 | `a.log` readable, `nope.log` missing | `python -m logredact --out-dir clean a.log nope.log` | *(empty)* | diagnostic naming `nope.log` | 2 |
+| 14 | two readable files | `python -m logredact --count --out-dir clean a.log b.log` | `wrote 2 files\n` | one four-field summary line | 0 |
+| 15 | no operands | `python -m logredact --out-dir clean` | *(empty)* | `logredact: --out-dir requires at least one FILE\n`; `clean` not created | 2 |
+| 16 | `clean` exists as a regular file, `a.log` readable | `python -m logredact --out-dir clean a.log` | *(empty)* | diagnostic naming `clean` | 2 |
+
+In row 13 note that `clean/a.log` **is** present on disk (the first operand succeeded) while stdout
+is empty — the status line is suppressed, not the completed work.
+
+## Requirement coverage map
+
+Every functional requirement maps to the test file that must name it (Principle III, SC-002). 001's
+map stays valid for its own requirements; `tests/test_count.py` and the three files marked below also
+change for the amended tally.
+
+| Requirement | Covered by |
+|-------------|-----------|
+| FR-001 `[PHONE]` replacement | `tests/test_phone.py`, `tests/test_redact_line.py` |
+| FR-002 `+` then 8–15 digits, boundaries included | `tests/test_phone.py` |
+| FR-003 runs outside the range wholly unchanged, no fragment | `tests/test_phone.py` |
+| FR-004 every occurrence; precedence vs email / IPv4 / card | `tests/test_phone.py`, `tests/test_redact_line.py` |
+| FR-005 existing three categories byte-identical | `tests/test_redact_line.py`, `tests/test_fidelity.py` |
+| FR-006 four-field summary format and totals | `tests/test_count.py` |
+| FR-007 summary on stderr, after output, absent without `--count`, absent on failure | `tests/test_count.py`, `tests/test_errors.py` |
+| FR-008 `--out-dir` redirects per operand | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-009 output named from the operand's basename | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-010 `DIR` and parents created; existing `DIR` used as-is | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-011 existing file fully replaced | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-012 `wrote N files`, once, after all writes | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-013 no redacted text on stdout in output-folder mode | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-014 output file byte fidelity equals the stdout path | `tests/test_out_dir.py`, `tests/test_fidelity.py` |
+| FR-015 unreadable `FILE`: name, reason, exit 2, no status line, no summary | `tests/test_out_dir_errors.py` |
+| FR-016 no output for a failed operand; earlier outputs kept | `tests/test_out_dir_errors.py` |
+| FR-017 uncreatable `DIR` / unwritable output: path, reason, exit 2 | `tests/test_out_dir_errors.py` |
+| FR-018 `--out-dir` with zero operands | `tests/test_out_dir_errors.py` |
+| FR-019 `--out-dir` in any position, with/without `--count` | `tests/test_out_dir.py`, `tests/test_count.py` |
+| FR-020 operands never modified | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
+| FR-021 exit 0 on full success | `tests/test_out_dir.py` |
